/*Q14. Write a Java program to find the product with the lowest price among three products.
Define a class Product with the following instance variables:
• pcode (int): stores the product code.
• pname (String): stores the product name.
• price (double): stores the product price.
Implement a parameterized constructor in the Product class to initialize all three instance variables.
The LowestPriceProduct class must perform the following operations:
1. Create an array to store three Product objects.
2 Read the product code, product name, and product price for each product.
3. Create a Product object for each set of input values and store it in the array.
4. Compare the prices of the three products and identify the product with the lowest price. If multiple products have the same lowest
price, select the first one.
5: Display the details of the lowest-priced product in the required output format.
Input Format:
Enter the details of three products, one product after another. For each product, provide the following values on separate lines:
• Product code (integer)
• Product name (string)
• Price (double)
Output Format:
Print the product details of the product with the lowest price in the following format:
Lowest priced product:
Product Code: <pcode>
Product Name: <pname>
Product Price: <price>
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
class Product {
    int pcode;
    String pname;
    double price;
 
    Product(int pcode, String pname, double price) {
        this.pcode = pcode;
        this.pname = pname;
        this.price = price;
    }
}
 
public class LowestPriceProduct {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        Product[] products = new Product[3];
        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
            int code = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
            String name = sc.nextLine().trim();
            double price = Double.parseDouble(sc.nextLine().trim());
            products[i] = new Product(code, name, price);
        }
        Product low = products[0];
        for (int i = 1; i < 3; i++) {
            if (products[i].price < low.price) {   // first one wins on a tie
                low = products[i];
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Lowest priced product:");
        System.out.println("Product Code: " + low.pcode);
        System.out.println("Product Name: " + low.pname);
        System.out.println("Product Price: " + low.price);
        sc.close();
    }
}
